@page "/admin/api"
@rendermode RenderMode.InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = Wms.Core.MenuKeys.ADMIN_API)]

<PageTitle>WMS — API</PageTitle>

<div class="aiwms-page-header">
    <h2>API</h2>
    <p>REST API exposed by WMS for machine-to-machine integrations. Manage credentials under <a href="/admin/api/client-apps">Client Apps</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class="aiwms-card">
    <div class="aiwms-card-header">Base URL</div>
    <table class="aiwms-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Environment</th><th>URL</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Production</td><td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">https://bflwms.bflgroup.ae/api/v1</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Local dev</td><td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">http://localhost:5217/api/v1</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">The <code>v1</code> segment is a versioned path — a future breaking change ships as <code>/api/v2</code> alongside it, rather than breaking existing clients.</p>
</div>

<div class="aiwms-card">
    <div class="aiwms-card-header">Authentication — OAuth2 client-credentials grant</div>
    <p>Every client app (created under <a href="/admin/api/client-apps">Client Apps</a>) gets a <code>client_id</code> and a <code>client_secret</code>, shown once at creation. Exchange them for a short-lived bearer token, then send that token on every call.</p>

    <p style="margin-top:16px"><strong>1. Request a token</strong> — form-encoded POST, no auth required:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">POST /api/v1/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&amp;client_id=&lt;id&gt;&amp;client_secret=&lt;secret&gt;</pre>

    <p style="margin-top:12px"><strong>Response:</strong></p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">{
  "access_token": "eyJhbGciOi...",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "expires_in": 3600
}</pre>

    <p style="margin-top:16px"><strong>2. Call a protected endpoint</strong> — send the token as a bearer header:</p>
    <pre style="background:var(--bfl-grey-900);color:#e4e4e0;padding:14px 16px;border-radius:var(--r-sm);font-family:Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;overflow-x:auto">GET /api/v1/ping
Authorization: Bearer &lt;access_token&gt;</pre>

    <p style="margin-top:12px;font-size:12px;color:var(--text-secondary)">Tokens expire after 1 hour by default. Revoking a client app in <a href="/admin/api/client-apps">Client Apps</a> immediately stops new tokens from being issued for it (existing tokens remain valid until they expire).</p>
</div>

<div class="aiwms-card">
    <div class="aiwms-card-header">Endpoints</div>
    <table class="aiwms-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>Auth</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier2">POST</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/oauth/token</td>
                <td>None</td>
                <td>Exchange a client_id/client_secret for a bearer token (client-credentials grant).</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier1">GET</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/ping</td>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier3">Bearer token</span></td>
                <td>Sample protected endpoint — returns the calling client_id and server time.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><span class="aiwms-pill tier1">GET</span></td>
                <td style="font-family:Consolas,monospace">/api/v1/ping/anonymous</td>
                <td>None</td>
                <td>Sample open endpoint — for connectivity testing without credentials.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>
